  "discussion": {
    "headline": "dry, tranquil and beautiful autumn weather to last into next week",
    "dateLine": "Brief 11:30 a.m. Friday, October 23, 2026, Update",
    "excerpt": "This week's weather has been nothing short of spectacular across the mid-Atlantic States, and the gorgeous conditions will be here for an \"extended stay\" through most if not all of next week. Behind Thursday night's weak cold frontal passage, light, northeasterly winds of 6-12 mph will usher slightly cooler and even drier air into the Commonwealth today. However, high temperatures will still reach the low 60s.. or just 2-3°F below average.. …",
